On Dec 4, 6:10 pm, Jorgen Grahn <grahn+n...@snipabacken.se> wrote:
> Are there tricks to uncurse a cursed BoH which is too heavy to lift,
> other than the ones listed at the wiki? Namely: (a) cancel it (b) let
> a gelatinous cube eat it.

I can think of one other option, albeit a rather fatalistic one.

If you loot the bag, *some* of its contents will be destroyed, which
will
make it lighter.  Hopefully then you'll be able to lift it and dip it
in holy
water.  There are two ways to do this:  the less efficient way is to
loot
the bag repeatedly, then pick it up and dip it.  The better way is to
drop
everything else you're carrying and loot the bag just once, taking out
as
much as you can of what's left, focusing on taking out the heaviest
items if possible, in the hopes that you will then be able to lift the
bag
and not have to loot it again (until it's uncursed).

This is, granted, a less-than-ideal option.  In all probability some
of the
most desirable contents would be lost.  It would also virtually
guarantee
that you'd find a wand of cancellation a short while later, because
the RNG
is mean like that.  But if you absolutely can't do anything else
useful with
it, and you reach a point where you no longer see any value in leaving
it
for later (when you, perhaps, find a wind of cancellation), the option
is
there.  Worst case scenario, the desirable contents would be destroyed
but you would be able to recover the bag of holding itself.  Empty,
it
would be easy to lift and dip in holy water.  Then you'd have a bag
of
holding that you currently don't have.

But yeah, I'd tend to want to wait for a wand of cancellation if
possible.

What will it take for you to get the castle wand?  I know it seems odd
to wish for a wand of cancellation, but weigh the value of everything
you'd be getting from the bag of holding against what else you could
wish for.


